From 5ce4da4b5e94fa7be1dac3230bbb6eee65310ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] filesystem/posix: a folder that readdir() could not read to
 its end is reported, not listed short

readdir() returns NULL both at the end of a directory and when it fails, and
only errno tells them apart. CPosixDirectory::GetDirectory() looked at the
pointer alone, so a file system that cannot read a part of a directory gave
a folder that looks complete and lacks files, with nothing in the log. The
kernel front (linux-9918) made a damaged index of NTFS return EIO instead of
a silent short listing; this makes Kodi say so.

ReadNextDirEntry() (DirEntry.h) clears errno, calls readdir() and returns the
errno of a failed call, 0 at the end. GetDirectory() logs the folder, the
number of entries read before the failure and the error, returns false (what
was read is not shown), and, where the caller allows prompting, shows an error
dialog in plain language with the reason. RemoveRecursive() does not remove a
folder it could not read to its end, and logs it.

Tested on the host with a readdir() that is scripted to end or to fail with
EIO or EACCES after n entries (6 cases) and with two mutants of the header
(errno not cleared, errno ignored): the test fails on both.

Strings: core #41800 (English), Estuary #33800 (English, es_es, es_ar,
es_mx).
